Montopolis Area Targeting Strategy

Area Overview

Montopolis is a neighborhood in Southeast Austin, one of the last affordable neighborhoods close to downtown Austin. The community has strong historical roots as one of Austin's oldest African American neighborhoods and continues to be home to many long-term residents and working families. Located along Riverside Drive near the Colorado River, Montopolis is experiencing development pressure as Austin's affordability crisis pushes development further southeast.

The neighborhood has significant infrastructure needs and represents an important market for basic electrical safety and modernization work. Montopolis Community Center and local churches are important community anchors. The area is also seeing new development and investment as land values rise throughout Austin.

Demographics & Property Profile

Median Home Value: $300,000-$500,000 (rapidly rising from historical lows)
Predominant Age Range: 25-65 (diverse, many long-term residents)
Household Income: $30,000-$75,000
Education Level: 45-65% with Bachelor's degrees
Property Types: Small historic homes, mobile homes, duplexes, some new development
Home Ages: Mix of 1940s-1980s original homes with some newer construction

Primary Services to Highlight

